Package: multiCollglm
Type: Package
Title: Collinearity Diagnostics for Generalized Linear Models
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Catalina", family = "Garcia Garcia",
           email = "cbgarcia@go.ugr.es", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person(given = "Roman", family = "Salmeron Gomez", role = "aut")
    )
Description: Tools to diagnose collinearity in generalized linear models
    (GLMs) via the condition number, a full Belsley-Kuh-Welsch variance-
    decomposition analysis, and the Redefined Variance Inflation Factor
    (RVIF; Salmeron, Garcia and Garcia 2025). All three are computed on
    the design matrix weighted by the IRLS weights at convergence and
    scaled to unit length by column (without centering). condition_number()
    additionally supports five condition-number definitions via its
    'method' argument: no transformation at all ('"RAW"'), Mackinnon and
    Puterman (1989) ('"MP"'), Marx and Smith (1990) ('"MS"'), Weissfeld
    and Sereika (1991) ('"WS"', the package default), and Ozkale (2019)
    ('"OZ"'). ml_collinearity() implements the diagnostic of Lesaffre and
    Marx (1993), comparing the condition number of the original design
    matrix (via 'multiColl''s CNs()) against Mackinnon and Puterman's
    (1989) condition number of the information matrix to distinguish
    ordinary collinearity from ML-collinearity. Provides methods for
    'glm' objects and for regularized models fitted with 'glmnet' or
    'cv.glmnet', which are internally refit as a 'glm' on the active set
    of variables selected at the given lambda.
    Ships four example datasets (Nitrogen, Mine, LeeCancer, Plastic) used
    by the package's reproduction articles, which reproduce and compare
    against condition numbers reported in the published literature.
